Subject: Share original frontend scene catalog and lifecycle ordering
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84

Retain all107 original scene IDs and filenames in a shared initializer; extract
unchanged scene enums/record and original enqueue, stack insertion, initialize,
resource-unload order and readiness/render predicates. Native ownership uses
checked typed FEN storage and explicit handler/publication readiness. Original
state6 and resource completion, concrete handlers and binary relocation remain
console behavior; no native success provider or factory is supplied.

Refreshed for decomp 9046e67a: feSceneManager.cpp keeps its upstream text (0147
restored it anyway). FrontendSceneEntries.inc now holds upstream's scene table
with its STRIKER_TIMES_SCENE_FILE (defined there when the includer has not).

